#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook (thesis repo only): keeps the adversarial ICLR-spotlight
# reviewer in play WITHOUT Lokesh having to ask for it (standing request,
# 2026-07-22). Emits a one-line reminder when the prompt looks like a research
# decision; silent otherwise so it never taxes mechanical turns.
#
# 2026-08-01: once the keyword screen fires, the reminder itself is written by a
# pi subagent (`pi-nudge`) that sees only the prompt — so it can name the actual
# decision being made instead of reciting the gate. The screen stays a bash case
# statement, so the no-op path is unchanged and still <1s.
#
# Contract: stdin = JSON event payload; stdout = context injected for the model.
# Must stay <1s on the no-op path.
set -uo pipefail

BIN="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
payload="$(cat 2>/dev/null || true)"

# Only for the thesis repo.
case "${PWD:-}" in
  *Research/LiteratureSurvey*) ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;
esac

# Cheap keyword screen over the prompt text (no jq dependency).
# NOTE (2026-07-24): the pure-presentation triggers (paper/present/report) were
# removed so authoring work is not auto-nagged. Genuine research-decision keywords
# still fire; anything narrower is summoned on demand with the `/critic` command
# (Claude) or `just critic` (pi).
prompt="$(printf '%s' "$payload" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
case "$prompt" in
  *experiment*|*baseline*|*benchmark*|*ablation*|*claim*|*result*|*metric*|\
  *scenario*|*seed*|*iclr*|*spotlight*|*novel*|\
  *contribution*|*evaluat*|*sufficient*|*enough*|*conclude*|*shows*|*proves*|\
  *significan*|*compare*|*sota*|*state-of-the-art*|*reviewer*)
    fallback="$(cat <<'EOF'
[research-gate] This turn touches a research decision. Per Lokesh's standing
requests, invoke the `research` skill and run its gate BEFORE acting on or
reporting the decision:
  1. theorist (research/references/theorist.md) — what existing theory predicts
     this outcome, or the NOVEL falsifiable hypothesis the experiment will
     prove/disprove (novelty checked against the literature graph + the
     hypothesis ledger). No hypothesis => not a severe test => send it back.
  2. critic (research/references/critic.md) — adversarial ICLR-spotlight review
     as a subagent; for an experiment plan this is a HARD GATE (no compute until
     cleared as a severe test whose failure is as informative as its success).
Report the hypothesis, the top objections, and their cost to fix. Do not
suppress an inconvenient critique. (To summon this gate yourself at any time:
`/critic` in Claude, `just critic` in pi.)
EOF
)"
    # Only the prompt is handed over — no repo state, no session, no skills.
    ctx="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/research-critic-ctx.XXXXXX")"
    trap 'rm -f "$ctx"' EXIT
    printf '%s' "$payload" | head -c 8000 >"$ctx"

    # UserPromptSubmit blocks the turn from starting, so this one is kept on a
    # tighter budget than the Stop nudges: a slow gate reminder is worse than a
    # generic one.
    PI_NUDGE_TIMEOUT="${PI_NUDGE_TIMEOUT:-25}" \
    PI_NUDGE_TASK='You are the research-gate hook for Lokesh'"'"'s thesis repo. The JSON payload
below contains the prompt he just submitted. A keyword screen flagged it as
possibly a research decision.

If it really is one — a claim, an experiment plan, a baseline/ablation choice,
an evaluation, a conclusion drawn from results — reply with at most 5 lines
telling the agent to run the research gate BEFORE acting: theorist first (what
existing theory predicts, or the novel falsifiable hypothesis, novelty-checked
against the literature graph and hypothesis ledger; no hypothesis means no
severe test), then critic (adversarial ICLR-spotlight review; a HARD GATE for an
experiment plan — no compute until cleared). Name the specific decision in his
prompt so the reminder is about his actual question, and say what the hypothesis
would have to be. Never tell him to suppress an inconvenient critique.

If the keyword matched something mechanical — editing prose, fixing a build,
renaming a file, a formatting or tooling question that merely contains a
research word — reply with exactly: SILENT' \
      "$BIN/pi-nudge" research-gate - "$ctx" <<<"$fallback"
    ;;
esac
exit 0
